From be773a5a24dcc678fe6c5c89abb8f0468da5cf22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zibran Khan <kali834x@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:10:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] shaper: fix double free in get_reference_table

hb_blob_create takes ownership of the data it is handed: if it cannot
create the blob (the hb_blob_t allocation fails, or length >= 2^31),
it calls the destroy callback itself and returns the empty blob.
afc4fa357f turned the dead !blob check after it into an
hb_blob_is_immutable check, so on that path buf is now freed twice.

Return the result of hb_blob_create as is and leave buf to HarfBuzz.

Upstream: https://github.com/libass/libass/commit/be773a5a24dcc678fe6c5c89abb8f0468da5cf22
---
 libass/ass_shaper.c | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libass/ass_shaper.c b/libass/ass_shaper.c
index d733d5d..112c17c 100644
--- a/libass/ass_shaper.c
+++ b/libass/ass_shaper.c
@@ -291,11 +291,8 @@ get_reference_table(hb_face_t *hbface, hb_tag_t tag, void *font_data)
     return NULL;
   }
 
-  hb_blob_t *blob = hb_blob_create(buf, len, HB_MEMORY_MODE_WRITABLE, buf, free);
-  if (len > 0 && hb_blob_is_immutable(blob))
-      free(buf);
-
-  return blob;
+  // HarfBuzz frees buf itself if the blob cannot be created
+  return hb_blob_create(buf, len, HB_MEMORY_MODE_WRITABLE, buf, free);
 }
 
 static hb_bool_t
